# Modules allowed to name raw session capabilities (tools/capability_confinement_check.sh).
# One per line: <path from the repository root>: <why it must>.
# These are the two command-boundary modules (G08 Stage 2c-ii-d): they
# assemble traced providers and acquisitions for commands. Every other
# main-library or singular-command module imports the safe surface only.
offchain/cli/src/Singular/CLI/Session.hs: command boundary — assembles traced providers, acquisitions, submissions and confirmations for commands; the only CLI module that may name the raw provider
offchain/cli/src/Singular/CLI/Attached.hs: deployment-attach boundary — reads providers directly to attach to a deployment; same exception as Session
